---
/* How the projects relate: one fictional bank built in three tiers, plus the
   cloud tooling that stands on its own. Anything not yet built is drawn
   dashed and labelled planned, so the picture never overstates the estate. */
---

<figure class="estate" aria-labelledby="est-title">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 1240 520" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-describedby="est-desc">
    <title id="est-title">How the projects fit together</title>
    <desc id="est-desc">
      Biira Bank is built in three tiers. A public website on Cloudflare's edge, an identity estate of
      Active Directory federated to Okta and Entra ID, and the segmented network underneath both. Three
      cloud tools sit outside the bank: a posture dashboard for AWS and Azure, a cost optimiser, and an
      identity job scout.
    </desc>

    <defs>
      <marker id="e-ar" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8.5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0 0L10 5 0 10z" fill="currentColor" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    {/* the bank */}
    <g class="frame">
      <rect x="20" y="36" width="812" height="462" rx="14" />
      <text x="44" y="24" class="lab">Biira Bank, a fictional regulated bank</text>
    </g>

    {/* public tier */}
    <g class="tier web" style="--t:var(--c-cloud);--d:0s">
      <rect x="44" y="62" width="764" height="116" rx="10" />
      <text x="68" y="90" class="k">Public tier</text>
      <text x="68" y="116" class="h">biirabank.com</text>
      <text x="68" y="140" class="p">Static site on Cloudflare Workers. Strict transport, security headers,</text>
      <text x="68" y="158" class="p">no client-side scripting. Graded F to A+ by an independent checker.</text>
      <g class="chip"><rect x="606" y="96" width="180" height="26" rx="13" /><text x="696" y="113" class="c">What the internet can reach</text></g>
    </g>

    <path class="link dashed" d="M426 178 L426 210" marker-end="url(#e-ar)" style="--d:0.3s" />
    <text x="438" y="198" class="s">sign-in hands off to Okta, planned</text>

    {/* identity */}
    <g class="tier idn" style="--t:var(--c-identity);--d:0.2s">
      <rect x="44" y="212" width="764" height="126" rx="10" />
      <text x="68" y="240" class="k">Identity estate</text>
      <text x="68" y="266" class="h">corp.biirabank.com</text>
      <text x="68" y="290" class="p">Active Directory with a tiered admin model, federated to Okta and</text>
      <text x="68" y="308" class="p">Microsoft Entra ID. Conditional access by network zone, graduated MFA.</text>
      <text x="68" y="326" class="p sm">Forest rebuilt from a decision record. The Okta org is being rebuilt with Terraform.</text>
      <g class="chip"><rect x="606" y="252" width="180" height="26" rx="13" /><text x="696" y="269" class="c">Who may reach what</text></g>
    </g>

    <path class="link" d="M426 338 L426 370" marker-end="url(#e-ar)" style="--d:0.4s" />
    <text x="438" y="358" class="s">runs on</text>

    {/* network */}
    <g class="tier net" style="--t:var(--c-detection);--d:0.4s">
      <rect x="44" y="372" width="764" height="110" rx="10" />
      <text x="68" y="400" class="k">Network and detection</text>
      <text x="68" y="426" class="h">Six VLANs behind one default-deny firewall</text>
      <text x="68" y="450" class="p">Proxmox on a trunk port, a Wazuh SIEM with three agents, a Greenbone</text>
      <text x="68" y="468" class="p">scanner whose identity holds nothing on the domain.</text>
      <g class="chip"><rect x="606" y="412" width="180" height="26" rx="13" /><text x="696" y="429" class="c">What everything stands on</text></g>
    </g>

    {/* cloud tooling */}
    <g class="frame alt">
      <rect x="864" y="36" width="356" height="462" rx="14" />
      <text x="888" y="24" class="lab">Cloud tooling, built to stand alone</text>
    </g>

    <g class="tool" style="--t:var(--c-assessment);--d:0.6s">
      <rect x="888" y="62" width="308" height="116" rx="10" />
      <text x="910" y="90" class="k">Posture</text>
      <text x="910" y="116" class="h sm">Cloud Security Posture Dashboard</text>
      <text x="910" y="140" class="p">Terraform plants the misconfiguration,</text>
      <text x="910" y="158" class="p">Prowler and ScoutSuite find it.</text>
    </g>

    <g class="tool" style="--t:var(--c-assessment);--d:0.7s">
      <rect x="888" y="196" width="308" height="116" rx="10" />
      <text x="910" y="224" class="k">Cost</text>
      <text x="910" y="250" class="h sm">AWS Cost Optimizer</text>
      <text x="910" y="274" class="p">A read-only command line tool that</text>
      <text x="910" y="292" class="p">names the waste and never touches it.</text>
    </g>

    <g class="tool" style="--t:var(--c-assessment);--d:0.8s">
      <rect x="888" y="330" width="308" height="116" rx="10" />
      <text x="910" y="358" class="k">Identity careers</text>
      <text x="910" y="384" class="h sm">IAM Job Scout</text>
      <text x="910" y="408" class="p">Collects identity roles, scores them,</text>
      <text x="910" y="426" class="p">and reports on the market it sees.</text>
    </g>
  </svg>

  <figcaption>
    One bank in three tiers, and the cloud tools beside it. Every tier has a case study, a repository and its
    evidence. Anything dashed is planned rather than built.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .estate { margin: 0 0 3rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .estate svg { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; overflow: visible; }

  .estate .frame rect { fill: none; stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-dasharray: 3 4; }
  .estate .lab { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; fill: var(--ink-3); }

  .estate .tier rect, .estate .tool rect { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--t); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .estate .tier > rect, .estate .tool > rect { filter: none; }
  .estate .k { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; fill: var(--t); }
  .estate .h { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 22px; fill: var(--ink); }
  .estate .h.sm { font-size: 18px; }
  .estate .p { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--ink-2); }
  .estate .p.sm { font-size: 11px; fill: var(--ink-3); }
  .estate .s { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; fill: var(--ink-3); }
  .estate .c { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 9.5px; fill: var(--t); text-anchor: middle; }
  .estate .chip rect { fill: none; stroke: var(--t); stroke-width: 1; opacity: 0.6; }

  .estate .link { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink-3); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .estate .link.dashed { stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }

  .estate figcaption { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--ink-3); margin-top: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.5; }

  .estate .tier, .estate .tool { opacity: 0; animation: est-fade 0.5s ease-out forwards; animation-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .estate .link { stroke-dasharray: 60; stroke-dashoffset: 60; animation: est-draw 0.5s ease-out forwards; animation-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .estate .link.dashed { animation-name: est-draw-dashed; }
  @keyframes est-draw { to { stroke-dashoffset: 0; } }
  @keyframes est-draw-dashed { to { stroke-dashoffset: 0; } }
  @keyframes est-fade { to { opacity: 1; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .estate .tier, .estate .tool { opacity: 1; animation: none; }
    .estate .link { stroke-dashoffset: 0; animation: none; }
    .estate .link.dashed { stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .estate { display: none; } }
</style>
